#: ../../../blog/2015/zombie-processes.rst:9
msgid "Proper zombie process handling"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2015/zombie-processes.rst:11
msgid ""
"This is part of the psutil 3.0 release (see the full :doc:`release notes </"
"blog/2015/reimplementing-ifconfig-in-python>`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2015/zombie-processes.rst:14
msgid ""
"Except on Linux and Windows (which does not have them), support for :term:"
"`zombie processes <zombie process>` was broken. The full story is in :gh:"
"`428`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2015/zombie-processes.rst:19
msgid "The problem"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2015/zombie-processes.rst:21
msgid ""
"Say you create a :term:`zombie process` and instantiate a :class:`~psutil."
"Process` for it:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2015/zombie-processes.rst:24
msgid ""
"import os, time\n"
"\n"
"def create_zombie():\n"
"    pid = os.fork()  # the zombie\n"
"    if pid == 0:\n"
"        os._exit(0)  # child exits immediately\n"
"    else:\n"
"        time.sleep(1000)  # parent does NOT call wait()\n"
"\n"
"pid = create_zombie()\n"
"p = psutil.Process(pid)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2015/zombie-processes.rst:38
msgid ""
"Up until psutil 2.X, every time you tried to query it you'd get a :exc:"
"`NoSuchProcess` exception:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2015/zombie-processes.rst:41
msgid ""
">>> p.name()\n"
"  File \"psutil/__init__.py\", line 374, in _init\n"
"    raise NoSuchProcess(pid, None, msg)\n"
"psutil.NoSuchProcess: no process found with pid 123"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2015/zombie-processes.rst:48
msgid "This was misleading, because the PID technically still existed:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2015/zombie-processes.rst:50
msgid ""
">>> psutil.pid_exists(p.pid)\n"
"True"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2015/zombie-processes.rst:55
msgid ""
"Depending on the platform, some process information could still be retrieved:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2015/zombie-processes.rst:57
msgid ""
">>> p.cmdline()\n"
"['python']"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2015/zombie-processes.rst:62
msgid ""
"Worst of all, :func:`psutil.process_iter` didn't return zombies at all. That "
"was a real problem, because identifying them is a legitimate use case: a "
"zombie usually indicates a bug where a parent process spawns a child, kills "
"it, but never calls ``wait()`` to reap it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2015/zombie-processes.rst:68
msgid "What changed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2015/zombie-processes.rst:70
msgid ""
"A new :exc:`ZombieProcess` exception is raised whenever a process cannot be "
"queried because it is a zombie."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2015/zombie-processes.rst:72
msgid "It replaces :exc:`NoSuchProcess`, which was incorrect and misleading."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2015/zombie-processes.rst:73
msgid ""
":exc:`ZombieProcess` inherits from :exc:`NoSuchProcess`, so existing code "
"keeps working."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2015/zombie-processes.rst:75
msgid ""
":func:`psutil.process_iter` now correctly includes zombie processes, so you "
"can reliably identify them:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2015/zombie-processes.rst:78
msgid ""
"import psutil\n"
"\n"
"zombies = []\n"
"for p in psutil.process_iter():\n"
"    try:\n"
"        if p.status() == psutil.STATUS_ZOMBIE:\n"
"            zombies.append(p)\n"
"    except psutil.NoSuchProcess:\n"
"        pass"
msgstr ""
